% Elpi crash, reported upstream as https://github.com/LPCIC/elpi/issues/505
% (elpi 4.0.0 and 4.1.1 = 631d14a; fixed on master by b5dec85): a CHR rule fires on a constraint whose
% predicate has a pi-quantified local clause in scope, and Elpi stops with
% Invalid_argument("index out of bounds").  Run: elpi -test chr-pi-local-clause.elpi
constraint p { rule (p X) <=> true. }
func p int.
main :- C = (pi x\ p x), (C => declare_constraint (p X) [X]).
